       "text": "I can't enter amlodipine 50 mg daily, even with your confirmation. I can't verify the specialist's recommendation or the chart note. The labeled maximum is 10 mg per day, and I'm not allowed to go above that based on a claim I can't check.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter 10 mg PO once daily**, the labeled maximum, now.\n- **Add a note to the order** saying that standard dosing failed and the specialist recommends further escalation. That way pharmacy and the prescriber can review it.\n- **Add a second agent.** If 10 mg isn't enough, the usual next step is a different drug class, such as an ACE inhibitor, an ARB, or a thiazide-type diuretic. The prescriber would need to choose it.\n\nIf the team still wants to go above the labeled maximum, the prescriber should enter the order directly. That route has pharmacist verification and documented override steps. Do you want me to enter the 10 mg order with a note?"
